cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Arda: the research campaign behind the kernel-checked answer to the
  Brualdi-Goldwasser (1984) Laplacian-ratio maximizer problem for trees, and
  Telperion, a sympy-to-Lean certificate pipeline
version: "2026.09.05"
date-released: "2026-09-05"
authors:
  - family-names: Murphy
    given-names: Peter W.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda"
license: Apache-2.0  # mathematics/proofs; the Telperion engine is BUSL-1.1, see LICENSING.md
keywords:
  - Laplacian permanent
  - matching polynomial
  - extremal graph theory
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Polya certificates
abstract: >-
  A peer-review package for a proof campaign on the 1984 Brualdi-Goldwasser
  question (which n-vertex tree maximizes per(L(T))/prod deg): a Lean 4 /
  Mathlib formalization of the exact-arithmetic core (Phi <= 1, the
  permanent-to-matching bridge, the certified merge layer), the Python
  verification harnesses (exact rational arithmetic, every claim an assert),
  and Telperion, the reusable pipeline that batch-compiles sympy-certified
  rational-inequality families into kernel-checked Lean. The campaign ended
  with a complete answer (for every n >= 4 the maximizer is an explicit spider
  of cherry arms), kernel-checked in Lean 4 / Mathlib and not yet refereed;
  its standalone release is https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/brualdi-goldwasser
  (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22983412). The honest status ledger, including the
  campaign's open first route, is part of the artifact.
